<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 7.2 percent.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 7.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose an adjusted 7.2 percent in the week to January 15 over the equivalent year-ago week, the Bank of England said.</p>
<p>Last week the annual adjusted rise was 8.1 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week  pvs week	yr-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     20.795	  21.38	   19.39</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	   2.084	   1.96	    1.81</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 7715</p>
